{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BASELINE: make lint clean in worktree at origin/main 024a6a227813 (all 25 checks + zizmor + actionlint pass).\n\nRECON (cream-capitate-snake / MCP<->library parity): 65 MCP tools across 3 registrars\n(_mcp_reads.py 35, _mcp_llm.py 7, _mcp_writes.py 23), declared as closures decorated\n@mcp.tool inside register_*_tools(mcp, ctx). Enumerable via FastMCP _tool_manager._tools;\nper-Tool: .name .fn .parameters(JSON schema) .output_schema .description .annotations .is_async.\nLibrary facade = src/rebar/__init__.py __all__ (~85 names, :173-262). 35 tool names match a\nfacade name exactly; remainder resolvable via [n for n in t.fn.__code__.co_names if n in __all__].\nConfirmed intentional divergence: library edit_ticket(ticket_id,*,repo_root,**fields) vs MCP\nedit_ticket with 11 enumerated params (_mcp_writes.py:360-372), self-documented at :383-385.\nPrecedent to imitate: scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py (parity gate w/ module-level waiver\nfrozenset + ::error:: output). gen_api_surface.py is a SNAPSHOT differ run from pytest, NOT in\nmake lint; new script is the right call.\n\nDESIGN DECISION (deviates from recon's baseline-free proposal): AC1+AC3 require a COMMITTED\nmanifest with a per-divergence reason field, so the gate is a hybrid — normalized manifest\ncommitted + --check/--update, undeclared divergence fails. Recon proposed a relational\ninvariant with no artifact; ticket ACs win."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788312806862094001,"uuid":"c20e2fbf-7f7d-4b11-bb24-d42211b44cd6"}